{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793400887,"nonce":"5nbgYXrOsQs++/4xRFVwfw5Rldw=","message":"Egress allowlist is now mapped for MSB (rayde_runner::Msb, commit after 8663f7c): Network::Allow(hosts) becomes --no-net plus one --net-rule allow@\u003chost\u003e per entry (names, *.suffix, IPs, CIDRs; entries that could add rule tokens are refused as Invalid), and the backend advertises network_allowlist. Verified live on the NUC with MSB 0.7.11: with allow@example.com the guest connects to example.com:443, any other name fails to resolve (the gateway DNS answers NXDOMAIN), and a raw IP (1.1.1.1:443) is blocked; the new ignored test msb_allowlist_blocks_other_hosts checks exactly that and passes, and msb_conforms still passes with its new allowlist checks. Limits: rules cover all ports and protocols of a host; there is no per-port form in the trait yet (MSB's grammar has host:proto:ports). GPU and read-only mounts stay unmapped. This is the egress control the hosted agent runs need (nan8 8082634).","files":null}]}